Cargo.lock

# `corpus/` is a generated artifact, not source: cargo-fuzz scaffolds it into
# this file, and it belongs there. Seeds cannot be reviewed as a diff, encode
# host byte order, and drift silently when a wire format changes — and over
# equal-length runs they moved coverage 0-5%, because libFuzzer recovers a
# magic from comparison interception in seconds. An input worth keeping
# becomes a unit test beside the decoder; a token hint goes in `dicts/`.
#
# The http corpora are the exception, tracked and owned with the codec.
/corpus/*
!/corpus/http_chunked/
!/corpus/http_frame/
!/corpus/http_head/
# What a local run *adds* to those is still an artifact: libFuzzer names its
# own finds by SHA1, so ignore anything shaped like one.
/corpus/*/[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f]
